				<wikidot:authorName>INT_Translator</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4721888</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p><strong>Home Wiki:</strong> <a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/">La Fundación SCP/Spanish-Speaking Branch</a><br /> <strong>Original Article:</strong> <a href="http://lafundacionscp.wikidot.com/scp-es-029">SCP-ES-029: Óbito Mecánico Masivo</a><br /> <strong>Original Author:</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/revenantheimdall" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2352752&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1565869643" alt="RevenantHeimdall" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2352752)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/revenantheimdall" >RevenantHeimdall</a></span><br /> <strong>Image Attribution:</strong> <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tailings,_Lexington_Mine_-_NARA_-_298138.tif?uselang=es">Public Domain</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StateLibQld_1_153479_Industrial_machinery_in_a_factory_in_Brisbane,_ca._1915.jpg">Public Domain</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goslar_-_UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe_Rammelsberg_Erzaufbereitung_(Haus_A)_(04-2).jpg">CC BY SA 3.0</a>.<br /> <strong>Translator:</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/revenantheimdall" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2352752&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1565869643" alt="RevenantHeimdall" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2352752)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/revenantheimdall" >RevenantHeimdall</a></span><br /> <strong>Editor(s):</strong> <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yossileiner" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2199269&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1565869643" alt="YossiLeiner" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2199269)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/yossileiner" >YossiLeiner</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modulum" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3072585&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1565869643" alt="Modulum" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3072585)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modulum" >Modulum</a></span></p> </blockquote> <p>Note from the author:</p> <blockquote> <p>This SCP was written more than 3 years ago, when the Series III was developing, when I was a (even more) casual writer infatuated by the recent GoI formats and lore, especially the shaping of the CotBG history. As my second SCP, I tried to create something in my homelands about how GoIs can seize the opportunity of low Foundation assets to develop their operations.</p> <p>Sadly, the authors who gave me feedback on this piece are completely inactive as of today. So I thank them for their feedback whenever they are now, and to all the ES branch for their reception. Also thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=172464&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1565869643" alt="Dr Gears" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=172464)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" >Dr Gears</a></span> for the creation of the GoI and SCP-217, and the Rapid Nomenclature Shift GoI2014 team for granting us their vision of a more modern, expanded CotBG.</p> </blockquote> 
				 	]]>
